{"entities":[{"pmid":"6381653","text":"Levodopa","etype":"Chemical","mesh":"D007980","start":0,"end":8},{"pmid":"6381653","text":"dyskinesia","etype":"Disease","mesh":"D004409","start":17,"end":27},{"pmid":"6381653","text":"Levodopa","etype":"Chemical","mesh":"D007980","start":45,"end":53},{"pmid":"6381653","text":"dyskinesia","etype":"Disease","mesh":"D004409","start":62,"end":72},{"pmid":"6381653","text":"Parkinsonism","etype":"Disease","mesh":"D010302","start":107,"end":119},{"pmid":"6381653","text":"dystonic","etype":"Disease","mesh":"D020821","start":153,"end":161},{"pmid":"6381653","text":"levodopa","etype":"Chemical","mesh":"D007980","start":395,"end":403},{"pmid":"6381653","text":"dyskinesias","etype":"Disease","mesh":"D004409","start":412,"end":423},{"pmid":"6381653","text":"thalamic lesions","etype":"Disease","mesh":"D013786","start":427,"end":443},{"pmid":"6381653","text":"Parkinsonism","etype":"Disease","mesh":"D010302","start":482,"end":494}],"gold_relations":"levodopa | CID | dyskinesias","metrics":{"precision":0.25,"recall":1.0,"f1":0.4,"tp":1,"fp":3,"fn":0,"rel_precision":0.25,"rel_recall":1.0,"rel_f1":0.4,"rel_tp":1,"rel_fp":3,"rel_fn":0},"pmid":"6381653","relations":["D007980 | CID | D004421","D007980 | CID | D013786","D007980 | CID | D010302","D007980 | CID | D004409"],"text":"Levodopa-induced dyskinesia and thalamotomy. Levodopa-induced dyskinesia of the limbs in thirteen cases of Parkinsonism, which was choreic, ballistic or dystonic in type, was alleviated almost completely by stereotaxic surgery using a microelectrode technique for the ventralis oralis anterior and posterior nuclei of the thalamus, but much less by the ventralis intermedius nucleus. Control of levodopa-induced dyskinesias by thalamic lesions in the course of routine treatment of Parkinsonism is discussed."}